# Agent roles (Cursor)

The kit ships 22 roles under `.kilo/agents/<name>.md`. They are **viewpoints**, not slash commands.

## Preferred: get the role via MCP

Call **`agent_get {name}`** to fetch a role's full definition and follow it. Enumerate names with `capabilities` (or `skill_search`).

- Entry: **`wawoo-auto`** (routes non-trivial work via MCP first).
- Delivery/design/implementation/quality: delivery-lead, project-manager, product-owner, architect, implementer, qa-engineer, data, code-reviewer, code-skeptic, code-simplifier
- Security/ops/release: security-reviewer, compliance-reviewer, performance-reviewer, sre-operator, release-manager
- UI/docs: web-designer, frontend-specialist, accessibility-reviewer, docs-specialist, docs-localization-reviewer

## Optional: native subagents

Cursor can run a role in an isolated context as a **project subagent** at `.cursor/agents/<name>.md` (Cursor app, CLI, and cloud agents). Generate them with `python3 scripts/install_cursor_workspace.py` (project) or `python3 scripts/install_cursor_global.py` (user-level).

> User-level `~/.cursor/agents/` is read by the **Cursor desktop app** only; the CLI / ACP reads **project** `.cursor/agents/`. When there is no project subagent, use `agent_get` — the role content is identical.

## Without MCP

Read `@.kilo/agents/<role>.md` and apply that role's viewpoint.
